# Melder runtime cache storage (generated, python-tag specific).
# The cache root src/melder/__melder_cache__/ hosts one subdirectory per
# caching subsystem: __conjure_cache__/ (compiler artifact bundles) and
# __crystallizer_cache__/ (persisted checkpoint cached-items). The package
# markers (__melder_cache__.py and the per-subsystem marker modules) stay
# tracked; generated bundle/cache subdirectories are ignored. Test-emitted
# cache droppings in the source tree are covered until those tests move to
# tmp_path cache roots.
*.melc
src/melder/__melder_cache__/__conjure_cache__/*/
src/melder/__melder_cache__/__crystallizer_cache__/*/
src/melder/tests/integration/melder/spellbook/_cache_runtime_*/
tests/tests/unit/melder/utilities/_caching_system_tmp_*/

# Build-asset caches. Same rule as every other .melc: derived, never committed.
#
# `*.melc` above already covers these; the directories are listed only so the
# convention is discoverable from this file.
#
#     src/melder/__melder_cache__/__bind_guard__/
#     src/melder/__melder_cache__/__agent_documentation__/
#
# The COMMITTED truth for those two assets is not a .melc at all - it is
# src/melder/_build_assets/<asset>/manifest/<asset>_manifest.py, plain Python
# literals, tracked and reviewed. The cache is rebuilt from it on demand and is
# interpreter-specific (marshal carries no cross-version guarantee), which is
# exactly why it cannot be the artifact that ships.
src/melder/__melder_cache__/__bind_guard__/
src/melder/__melder_cache__/__agent_documentation__/
